{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Wtx3iSVUoGjChuNB9cAbNR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the project context carefully to understand the current state and determine what tasks to propose.\n\n## Project Summary\n\n**Problem**: go-unix-utils is an experiment in specification-driven development using Unix utilities as a test bed. It derives formal specifications from C source code, generates Go implementations from specs using AI, and verifies parity via differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: \n- `cmd/` - One package per utility with main.go and tests\n- `pkg/testutils/` - Differential testing harness\n\n\n- `pkg/sys/` - Syscall abstractions\n- `pkg/format/` - Output formatting\n- `pkg/hashutil/` - Hash/checksum shared code\n- `pkg/sizeparse/` - Size parsing\n- `pkg/encutil/` - Encoding utilities\n- `docs/specs/` - SRDs, use cases, test suites\n- `magefiles/` - Build automation\n\n**Current State**: Looking at the code status, release 00.0 has partial implementation with magefiles, sys, hashutil, sizeparse, and encutil already in place, while format hasn't been started yet.\n\nScanning through the release statuses, I see 01.2 (sponge) and 01.3 (du) are implemented, 02.0 tools are all done, 02.1 (tee) is complete, 02.2 (head and seq) are finished, and 03.0 (wc) is implemented. For 03.1, arch, hostname, and hostid are done but uname and nproc haven't started. Everything from 04.0 onward is untouched. I need to look more carefully at the requirement_states to understand which items are marked as ready for implementation versus already complete. I'm noticing a discrepancy — format and testutils show \"not started\" in code_status, but they're not appearing in requirement_states, which suggests either all their requirements are already complete or they weren't included in the data. The constraint is clear though: I should only propose tasks for